{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nfrom math import isqrt\n\ndef read_ints():\n    return list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nn, mod = read_ints()\nmem = [0] * (n + 1)\nmem[1] = 1\n\nfor i in range(2, n + 1):\n    root = isqrt(i)\n    cur = 1  # sum starts with mem[1] = 1 implicitly\n    \n    # Sum over divisors f where 2 <= f <= sqrt(i)\n    for f in range(2, root + 1):\n        cur = (cur + mem[i // f]) % mod\n    \n    # Handle intervals for q = i // j where j > sqrt(i)\n    be = i\n    for q in range(1, i // (root + 1) + 1):\n        nxt = i // (q + 1)\n        cur = (cur + (be - nxt) * mem[q]) % mod\n        be = nxt\n    \n    mem[i] = cur\n\nprint(mem[n])\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int mod = sc.nextInt();\n        \n        long[] mem = new long[n + 1];\n        mem[1] = 1;\n        \n        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n            int root = (int) Math.sqrt(i);\n            long cur = 1; // sum starts with mem[1] = 1 implicitly\n            \n            // Sum over divisors f where 2 <= f <= sqrt(i)\n            for (int f = 2; f <= root; f++) {\n                cur = (cur + mem[i / f]) % mod;\n            }\n            \n            // Handle intervals for q = i // j where j > sqrt(i)\n            int be = i;\n            int maxQ = i / (root + 1);\n            for (int q = 1; q <= maxQ; q++) {\n                int nxt = i / (q + 1);\n                cur = (cur + (long)(be - nxt) * mem[q]) % mod;\n                be = nxt;\n            }\n            \n            mem[i] = cur;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(mem[n]);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.056941103655845e-05, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.1934269170742482e-05, -2.753696753643453e-05, -0.04303222894668579, -0.05660134553909302, -5.602820692729438e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.8954096958623268e-05, -0.00020382710499688983, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -0.0030960743315517902, -2.861018856492592e-06, -0.00987135712057352, -4.911301948595792e-05, -4.529942543740617e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.149708886165172e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -6.687417771900073e-05, -0.18110233545303345, -1.311301275563892e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.006777428206988e-06, -4.887569048150908e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576272320060525e-06, -0.313265323638916, -0.03764495626091957, -3.671578815556131e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -4.410734163684538e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -7.033323527139146e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.9550132492440753e-05, -0.0052368370816111565, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.3486134111881256, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07,